See @AGENTS.md for the full context: how to build and run, the layout, the
conventions, the generated files that must not be hand-edited, and the specific
mistakes this codebase has already made and written up.

Two things worth repeating here because they are easy to get wrong:

- This is a freestanding i386 kernel. There is no libc and no runtime. Anything
  the code calls, something in `kernel/` defines.
- Build and test only through Docker: `dev` to build, `dev test` to verify.
  Never suggest installing a toolchain on the host.
